import GroupApproximation.Sofic.TorsionFreeFullMFRadical

/-!
# The frozen public endpoint of the defect-routing program

This module states the Main Theorem of the routing program in its final
public form, with no construction structures, endpoint wrappers, or
formalization vocabulary in the statement.

The two theorems in the first section are the ones the manuscript cites,
and they are held to the manuscript's own sentence, word for word: *it
suffices to construct a quotient `q : E' ↠ Q` subject to five conditions
— `Q` is finitely presented; `Q` has property `(T)`; `Q` is torsion-free;
`Q` is generated by two elements; and `q(N_comp) = Q`.  Given such a `q`,
the group `Q` is two-generated, finitely presented, torsion-free, Kazhdan,
and equal to its own MF radical, so every homomorphism from `Q` to a matrix
quotient is trivial, and every nontrivial quotient of `Q` likewise fails to
be MF.*

So their hypothesis is `Nonempty (FiveConditionRoutingData D)`, which
carries those five conditions and nothing else, and their conclusion is
that printed list and nothing more.  In particular they do **not** conclude
`Nontrivial Q`: the trivial group satisfies all five printed conditions, so
nontriviality is not available at that strength, and asserting it would be
asserting something the printed hypotheses do not give.  Nontriviality
appears exactly where the manuscript puts it — on the quotient `H` in
"every nontrivial quotient of `Q`".

The second section carries the strictly stronger statements, over
`DefectRoutingData`, whose survival field makes `Q` itself nontrivial and
hence itself non-MF.  The third section discharges that extra field from
the manuscript's own description of Hull's quotient as order-preserving, so
that the stronger conclusions rest on a printed property of the
construction rather than on an assumption.

The decisive open obligation of the program is unchanged: build the routing
data unconditionally.  Every formalization step should be judged by whether
it moves that discharge closer.  The statements below are the specification
frozen in advance: whatever the construction produces must land exactly
here, and nothing downstream may widen the interface.
-/

namespace GroupApproximation
namespace FullMFRadicalEndpoint

universe u

/-! ## The printed endpoint -/

/-- **The Main Theorem, frozen.**  The five printed conditions yield a
two-generated, finitely presented, torsion-free property-`(T)` group whose
literal CDE MF radical is everything — that is, a group "equal to its own
MF radical". -/
theorem exists_twoGenerated_finitelyPresented_torsionFree_kazhdan_fullMFRadical :
    ∀ {P : Type} {E : Type u} [Group P] [Group E]
      {D : FournierFacioDefectData P E}
      (_h : Nonempty (FiveConditionRoutingData.{u} D)),
      ∃ (Q : Type) (_ : Group Q) (_ : Countable Q),
        IsTwoGenerated Q ∧
        Group.IsFinitelyPresented Q ∧
        IsPowerTorsionFree Q ∧
        HasKazhdanPropertyT.{0, 0} Q ∧
        cdeMFResidual Q = ⊤ := by
  intro P E _ _ D h
  obtain ⟨R⟩ := h
  letI : Group R.Quotient := R.groupQuotient
  letI : Countable R.Quotient := R.quotientCountable
  exact ⟨R.Quotient, inferInstance, inferInstance, R.isTwoGenerated,
    R.finitelyPresented, R.torsionFree, R.kazhdan, R.cdeMFResidual_eq_top⟩

/-- **Hereditary form, frozen.**  The five printed conditions yield a group
with the same profile such that every homomorphism from it to a matrix
quotient — the unitary group of a genuine norm-matrix C-star corona — is
trivial, and every nontrivial quotient of it fails to be MF.

Nontriviality is demanded of the quotient `H`, exactly as in the printed
sentence "every nontrivial quotient of `Q` likewise fails to be MF"; no
survival hypothesis on `Q` is used or needed. -/
theorem exists_group_with_every_nontrivial_quotient_not_isCDEOperatorMF :
    ∀ {P : Type} {E : Type u} [Group P] [Group E]
      {D : FournierFacioDefectData P E}
      (_h : Nonempty (FiveConditionRoutingData.{u} D)),
      ∃ (Q : Type) (_ : Group Q) (_ : Countable Q),
        IsTwoGenerated Q ∧
        Group.IsFinitelyPresented Q ∧
        IsPowerTorsionFree Q ∧
        HasKazhdanPropertyT.{0, 0} Q ∧
        (∀ (X : ℕ → FiniteModel) (hne : ∀ n, Nonempty (X n)),
          letI := hne
          (∀ n, 0 < Fintype.card (X n)) →
            ∀ rho : Q →* unitary (NormMatrixCStarCorona (fun n ↦ X n)),
              rho = 1) ∧
        ∀ (H : Type) (_ : Group H) (_ : Countable H) (_ : Nontrivial H)
          (f : Q →* H),
          Function.Surjective f → ¬ IsCDEOperatorMF H := by
  intro P E _ _ D h
  obtain ⟨R⟩ := h
  letI : Group R.Quotient := R.groupQuotient
  letI : Countable R.Quotient := R.quotientCountable
  refine ⟨R.Quotient, inferInstance, inferInstance, R.isTwoGenerated,
    R.finitelyPresented, R.torsionFree, R.kazhdan, ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro X hne hX rho
    exact R.cdeCoronaRepresentation_eq_one X hX rho
  · intro H _ _ _ f hf
    exact R.quotient_not_isCDEOperatorMF f hf

/-! ## The strictly stronger layer

`DefectRoutingData` carries one field beyond the printed five: the
protected simple-factor element survives routing.  That is what makes the
routed group itself nontrivial, and therefore itself non-MF rather than
merely a group all of whose nontrivial quotients are non-MF.  These two
statements are not the ones the manuscript prints; they are kept because
they are strictly stronger and because the downstream library uses them. -/

/-- Routing data — the five printed conditions plus survival of the
protected element — yields a **nontrivial** two-generated, finitely
presented, torsion-free property-`(T)` group with full CDE MF radical. -/
theorem exists_nontrivial_twoGenerated_finitelyPresented_torsionFree_kazhdan_fullMFRadical :
    ∀ {P : Type} {E : Type u} [Group P] [Group E]
      {D : FournierFacioDefectData P E}
      (_h : Nonempty (DefectRoutingData.{u} D)),
      ∃ (Q : Type) (_ : Group Q) (_ : Countable Q),
        IsTwoGenerated Q ∧
        Group.IsFinitelyPresented Q ∧
        IsPowerTorsionFree Q ∧
        HasKazhdanPropertyT.{0, 0} Q ∧
        Nontrivial Q ∧
        cdeMFResidual Q = ⊤ := by
  intro P E _ _ D h
  obtain ⟨R⟩ := h
  letI : Group R.Quotient := R.groupQuotient
  letI : Countable R.Quotient := R.quotientCountable
  exact ⟨R.Quotient, inferInstance, inferInstance, R.isTwoGenerated,
    R.finitelyPresented, R.torsionFree, R.kazhdan, R.quotientNontrivial,
    R.cdeMFResidual_eq_top⟩

/-- Routing data yields a nontrivial group, with the same profile, all of
whose nontrivial quotients fail to be MF — in particular the group itself
is not MF, and it admits no nontrivial finite, residually finite, or MF
quotient of any kind. -/
theorem exists_nontrivial_group_with_every_nontrivial_quotient_not_isCDEOperatorMF :
    ∀ {P : Type} {E : Type u} [Group P] [Group E]
      {D : FournierFacioDefectData P E}
      (_h : Nonempty (DefectRoutingData.{u} D)),
      ∃ (Q : Type) (_ : Group Q) (_ : Countable Q),
        IsTwoGenerated Q ∧
        Group.IsFinitelyPresented Q ∧
        IsPowerTorsionFree Q ∧
        HasKazhdanPropertyT.{0, 0} Q ∧
        Nontrivial Q ∧
        ¬ IsCDEOperatorMF Q ∧
        ∀ (H : Type) (_ : Group H) (_ : Countable H) (_ : Nontrivial H)
          (f : Q →* H),
          Function.Surjective f → ¬ IsCDEOperatorMF H := by
  intro P E _ _ D h
  obtain ⟨R⟩ := h
  letI : Group R.Quotient := R.groupQuotient
  letI : Countable R.Quotient := R.quotientCountable
  refine ⟨R.Quotient, inferInstance, inferInstance, R.isTwoGenerated,
    R.finitelyPresented, R.torsionFree, R.kazhdan, R.quotientNontrivial,
    R.not_isCDEOperatorMF, ?_⟩
  intro H _ _ _ f hf
  exact R.quotient_not_isCDEOperatorMF f hf

/-! ## Order preservation discharges the extra field

The manuscript describes Hull's quotient as "obtained by adjoining finitely
many relators, preserves element orders, and restricts to a surjection from
`S`".  Reading that description as an interface, torsion-freeness of the
quotient and survival of the protected element are both consequences, so
the strictly stronger endpoint above is reached from a torsion-free source
and a printed property of the construction, with nothing assumed about
survival. -/

/-- An order-preserving routing of a torsion-free skeleton yields the
strong endpoint: a nontrivial two-generated finitely presented torsion-free
Kazhdan group equal to its own MF radical, all of whose nontrivial
quotients fail to be MF.  Neither torsion-freeness of the quotient nor
survival of the protected element is assumed here; both are proved in
`OrderPreservingRoutingData`. -/
theorem exists_nontrivial_fullMFRadical_of_orderPreservingRouting :
    ∀ {P : Type} {E : Type u} [Group P] [Group E]
      {D : FournierFacioDefectData P E}
      (_h : Nonempty (OrderPreservingRoutingData.{u} D)),
      ∃ (Q : Type) (_ : Group Q) (_ : Countable Q),
        IsTwoGenerated Q ∧
        Group.IsFinitelyPresented Q ∧
        IsPowerTorsionFree Q ∧
        HasKazhdanPropertyT.{0, 0} Q ∧
        Nontrivial Q ∧
        cdeMFResidual Q = ⊤ ∧
        ∀ (H : Type) (_ : Group H) (_ : Countable H) (_ : Nontrivial H)
          (f : Q →* H),
          Function.Surjective f → ¬ IsCDEOperatorMF H := by
  intro P E _ _ D h
  obtain ⟨O⟩ := h
  obtain ⟨R⟩ : Nonempty (DefectRoutingData.{u} D) := ⟨O.toDefectRoutingData⟩
  letI : Group R.Quotient := R.groupQuotient
  letI : Countable R.Quotient := R.quotientCountable
  refine ⟨R.Quotient, inferInstance, inferInstance, R.isTwoGenerated,
    R.finitelyPresented, R.torsionFree, R.kazhdan, R.quotientNontrivial,
    R.cdeMFResidual_eq_top, ?_⟩
  intro H _ _ _ f hf
  exact R.quotient_not_isCDEOperatorMF f hf

end FullMFRadicalEndpoint
end GroupApproximation
